  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Designing the Login Screen**\n\nI\'m currently focused on the login screen design. I\'ve got the framework set for a CPF, birth date, and full name input. Verification will use a Google Sheet with ID `1uzQAAUN3dbmBK7p14cBTywTYuG3PNLiZVJtLRUtljnU` and the \"usu\303\241rios\" sheet. I need to integrate the logo too.\n\n\n**Analyzing Data Source Columns**\n\nI\'ve clarified the mapping between the login form fields and the Google Sheet columns, specifically D (full name), G (birth date), and N (CPF). The user confirmed these columns use masks. My plan is to use React to construct a frontend login form. I should start by fetching the logo, which is currently a landing page, so I need to find the direct image link or use the current link and test it.\n\n\n**Investigating Sheet Data Access**\n\nI\'m now prioritizing the data retrieval from the Google Sheet. I\'m exploring options: the Google Sheets API (requiring an API key) versus a public CSV/JSON export. I\'ve discovered a public JSON export URL: `https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1uzQAAUN3dbmBK7p14cBTywTYuG3PNLiZVJtLRUtljnU/gviz/tq?tqx=out:json&sheet=usu\303\241rios`. I am also working on handling the masks in the columns for CPF and birth date and thinking about frontend implementation using React, and backend (full-stack) to proxy the request if there are CORS issues. Alternatively, the client side should be ok if the sheet is public.\n\n\n**Defining Project Steps**\n\nMy current focus is on defining the concrete steps. I\'ve outlined the process: updating `metadata.json`, installing packages (maybe just a SPA), and fetching sheet data. UI will be built with Tailwind and Lucide icons. I\'m prioritizing the normalization logic to remove masks and lowercase strings for comparison. I\'ve also reconfirmed the data columns and started to determine the app name and description, and dependencies. Now I\'m checking if the sheet is accessible.\n\n\n**Choosing Data Fetching Method**\n\nI\'m leaning towards using `fetch` over `axios` for fetching sheet data, keeping things simple. I\'ll integrate `frontend-design` for a professional aesthetic. I have checked the logo link and I\'ll use a placeholder if I can\'t get the direct link. I\'ll move on to `frontend-design`, possibly including `shadcn-ui` if it enhances the UI. I have to adapt the prompt to Portuguese, or maintain the UI language. I have verified the columns with masks. I should probably remove non-digits from CPF and Birth Date for comparison. The main objective is to read `metadata.json`, update it with a project name like \"Login Seguro - Consulta Planilha\", and decide on installing `shadcn` for the UI.\n\n\n"
    modified_response: "Vou criar uma tela de login moderna e sofisticada utilizando React, Tailwind CSS e Framer Motion para as anima\303\247\303\265es. Como voc\303\252 solicitou a integra\303\247\303\243o com uma planilha Google, vou configurar o acesso aos dados da planilha e implementar a l\303\263gica de valida\303\247\303\243o comparando o Nome, Data de Nascimento e CPF, tratando as m\303\241scaras conforme mencionado.\n\nPrimeiro, vou atualizar os metadados do projeto e preparar os componentes.\n\n### Habilidades Relevantes\n- **[RELEVANTE]** frontend-design: usarei para criar uma interface limpa e profissional.\n- **[RELEVANTE]** shadcn-ui: usarei para componentes de formul\303\241rio e feedback de alta qualidade.\n\n---\n\n### Passo 1: Atualizar metadados e instalar depend\303\252ncias\nVou come\303\247ar atualizando o `metadata.json` e instalando pacotes \303\272teis para formul\303\241rios e m\303\241scaras.\n\n---\n\n### Passo 2: Implementar a L\303\263gica de Acesso \303\240 Planilha\nPara ler a planilha Google de forma p\303\272blica, usarei o endpoint `gviz/tq`, que retorna os dados em formato JSON. Aplicarei a normaliza\303\247\303\243o nos campos para garantir que o login funcione mesmo se o usu\303\241rio digitar com ou sem pontos/tra\303\247os.\n\nVamos come\303\247ar.\n\n"
    thinking_duration {
      seconds: 8
      nanos: 301051290
    }
    stop_reason: STOP_REASON_CLIENT_TOOL_PARSE_ERROR
  }
}
