    thinking: "**Refining Installment Display**\n\nI\'m currently working on displaying receivables more effectively in the dashboard, particularly focusing on how to handle installments (\"parcelas\"). My process involves identifying \"parcelada\" negotiations using Column P. I\'m starting from column A (PV/ID). The goal is to accurately represent multiple entries related to a single PV, which can show if the amount is parcelada or not.\n\n\n**Clarifying Data Column Usage**\n\nI\'m now zeroing in on data columns. Column P is crucial; it indicates if a negotiation is installment-based (\"parcelada\"). Specifically, it seems to indicate the total value of the \"parcelada\" negotiations. Column T previously seemed to be the \"receb\303\255veis\" column. I need to discern the \"status\" or the \"parcela\" number for each installment.\n\n\n**Pinpointing Payment Status**\n\nI am now focusing on determining the payment status of installments. I\'ve realized I need to identify which column indicates whether an installment is paid or available. The user\'s input suggests \"Pago\" or \"Dispon\303\255vel\" might be indicators. I\'m going to enhance the `fetchReceivables` function to include column P and potentially examine columns R, S, or U for status information, as they seem like likely candidates.\n\n\n**Identifying Installment Status**\n\nI\'m now investigating how to identify and represent installment status accurately. The user wants to see installment details like \"Parcela 1/5 - Pago\". I\'m focusing on finding columns for the total number of installments, the current installment number, and the payment status. I\'m fetching more columns around the receivables column, specifically examining columns P, Q, R, and S, and will update the `Receivable` interface to accommodate this additional data. My goal is to use the data to discern patterns like \"Pago,\" \"Recebido,\" or \"Aberto.\"\n\n\n"
    modified_response: "Para implementar a l\303\263gica de parcelamento, vamos ajustar o servi\303\247o para capturar a **coluna P** (que indica se est\303\241 parcelado ou \303\251 o valor total) e tentaremos identificar o status e a numera\303\247\303\243o das parcelas. \n\nTamb\303\251m agruparemos os receb\303\255veis pelo **ID (PV)** para apresentar a progress\303\243o das parcelas de forma organizada para o usu\303\241rio.\n\n### 1. Atualizando o Servi\303\247o de Dados\n\nVou expandir a interface `Receivable` para incluir a informa\303\247\303\243o de parcelamento e tentar capturar uma coluna de status (geralmente pr\303\263xima ao valor).\n\n```typescript\n// No arquivo sheetsService.ts\n```\n\n"
